{"packet_id":"D051-01","doc_id":"D051","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Notice to terminate a Massachusetts tenancy at will","requirement":"Either party may end a tenancy at will by giving the other three months' written notice; if rent is payable at periods shorter than three months, notice is sufficient if equal to the payment interval or thirty days, whichever is longer.","key_value":"3 months' notice; or payment interval / 30 days, whichever is longer","coverage_conditions":"Tenancies at will (no fixed term) in Massachusetts; the section governs how such estates may be determined and does not cover term tenancies.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"tenancies at will"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 12","quoted_span":"Estates at will may be determined by either party by three months' notice in writing for that purpose given to the other party; and, if the rent reserved is payable at periods of less than three months, the time of such notice shall be sufficient if it is equal to the interval between the days of payment or thirty days, whichever is longer.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D051-01","doc_id":"D051","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Notice to quit for nonpayment of rent and tenant's right to cure (tenancy at will)","requirement":"A landlord may end a tenancy at will for nonpayment of rent with fourteen days' written notice to quit; a tenant who has not received such a notice in the preceding twelve months may keep the tenancy by paying all rent due within ten days.","key_value":"14 days' notice to quit; 10-day right to cure","coverage_conditions":"Tenancies at will in Massachusetts where rent is neglected or refused; the cure right applies only if the tenant received no similar notice in the prior twelve months.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"tenancies at will"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":"If the notice omits the required cure notification, the tenant's cure period is extended to the day the answer is due in a possession action, but the notice is otherwise valid.","effective_date":null,"citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 12","quoted_span":"In case of neglect or refusal to pay the rent due from a tenant at will, fourteen days' notice to quit, given in writing by the landlord to the tenant, shall be sufficient to determine the tenancy;","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
